{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-44060","model_call":41,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"1984\" \"war is peace\" \"common enemy\" (+ unite united unity))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"1984\" \"war is peace\" \"common enemy\" (+ unite united unity))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_731902748#6_1459902809","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q855","rank":1,"snippet":"sharing information. Please try again later. Watch on 0:00 0:00 0:00 / 12:42 Live • MaudlinStreet Educator since 2009 857 answers | Certified Educator Page Citation Share Link This novel is constructed through paradox and contrasts. These three slogans of the Party reflect these aspects, in that the way the Party controls Oceania is actually the opposite of the propaganda it produces. Thus, according to the Party, \"war is peace\" means that they continually \"fight\" wars in order to keep peace at home. During times of war, nations generally <cover>unite. Of course, if the people are focused on a common enemy, they are much less inclined to notice how unhappy they are in their own lives. So they make less trouble for their government. \" Freedom is slavery\" can be thought of in the same way:\" , \"start_char\": 3843.000000 , \"title\": \"In 1984, what do these 3 slogans mean: War is Peace, </cover>Freedom is Slavery, and Ignorance is Strength?  - eNotes.com\" , \"url\": \"https://www.enotes.com/homework-help/in-1984-what-do-these-3-slogans-mean-war-is-peace-201861\" }"},"time":145},"model_calls":41,"document_judgments":29,"relevance_3":19,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
