{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-44060","model_call":42,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":19087,"output_tokens":235,"total_tokens":19322,"cached_tokens":18176,"reasoning_tokens":63},"output_characters":718,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_731902748#6_1459902809","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly explains that in 1984 the Party's slogan 'War is Peace' works because war makes nations unite, and people focused on a common enemy are less likely to notice their own misery or trouble the government. This directly supports hatred/opposition toward enemies as a unifying tool.","learned":"The Party uses war and common enemies to unite citizens, distract them from dissatisfaction, and keep them compliant."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q855","reason":"The War is Peace/common-enemy query is producing direct evidence about unity through opposition to enemies; continue for more grade-3 results."}}}
