{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-44060","model_call":42,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q855"},"model_calls":42,"document_judgments":30,"relevance_3":20,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-44060","model_call":42,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q855"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q855"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_822518523#2_1573293244","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q855","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_822518523#2_1573293244\" , \"end_char\": 1156.000000 , \"headings\": \" War is Peace. Freedom is Slavery. Ignorance is Strength. By: Monica Castro Leave a Reply Cancel reply \" , \"segment\": \"Freedom Is Slavery. Ignorance is Strength.” These are three slogans of the Party, Ingsoc. But what do they mean? “<cover>War is Peace” means that while Oceania is at war with other countries, the people will maintain united because they have a common enemy. Therefore, by keeping war, people don’t have enemies inside the country, because they are busy fighting enemies outside the country. In 1984, </cover>the war isn’t even necessary, but is kept as a means to control the people. The contradiction with this quote is that obviously war and peace are opposites. People can’t have peace when they feel threatened by a war, even if it is a foreign war. In 1984, people feel threatened by rocket bombs and Eurasian soldiers, when the real threat is the Party itself.\" , \"start_char\": 405.000000 ,"},"time":16},"model_calls":42,"document_judgments":30,"relevance_3":20,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
