{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-44060","model_call":53,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"1984\" \"unite the citizens\" \"common enemy\" (+ propaganda hate hatred))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"1984\" \"unite the citizens\" \"common enemy\" (+ propaganda hate hatred))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_332200854#3_753681491","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q858","rank":1,"snippet":"Goldstein’s] teaching” (Orwell 12), and consequently schedules Two Minute Hates (Orwell 2 Minutes of Hate) each day that feature videos of Goldstein speaking and the mobs of Party members expressing their deep hate of his teachings and their loyalty to the Party. In fact, the Hates work the citizens into such a nationalistic frenzy that “before the hate [s] had proceeded for thirty seconds, uncontrollable exclamations of rage were breaking out from half the people in the room” (Orwell 13). These overt forms of propaganda serve to <cover>unite the citizens against a common enemy and strengthen the sentiments of patriotism among Party members.\" , \"start_char\": 2935.000000 , \"title\": \"An Analysis of the Use of Propaganda in the Dystopian Societies Presented in The Handmaid’s Tale by Margaret Atwood, 1984 </cover>by George Orwell, and Fidel Castro’s Government in Cuba – Kylie's Blog\" , \"url\": \"https://kyliecblog.wordpress.com/2016/10/06/an-analysis-of-the-use-of-propaganda-in-the-dystopian-societies-presented-in-the-handmaids-tale-by-margaret-atwood-1984-by-george-orwell-and-fidel-castros-government-in-cuba/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_332200854#3_753681491","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":40},"model_calls":53,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":28,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
