{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-44060","model_call":62,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q863"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q863"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_758826587#7_1527251764","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q863","rank":6,"snippet":"1_doc_39_758826587#7_1527251764\" , \"end_char\": 6954.000000 , \"headings\": \"Two Minutes Hate 1984 1984 Two Minutes Hate <cover>1984 Expert Answers Further Reading We’ll help your grades soar \" , \"segment\": \"Although Winston does not believe all the lies about Goldstein and is not even sure that he exists, he finds that he does not need to pretend to hate the figure on the telescreen. After about thirty seconds, he feels a sense of passionate hatred for the figure on the screen and the words he hears, and he joins unaffectedly with the other Party members in their frenzy of hatred. The Party is therefore able to promote orthodoxy and cohesion at the same time. Last Updated by eNotes Editorial on November 30, 2020 marilynn07 Educator since 2009 469 answers | Certified Educator Page Citation Share Link The Two Minutes Hate is a ritual observance that is designed to use the collective </cover>rage of the people against supposed \"enemies of the Party\" to strengthen the Party's position among the people. The ritual serves to unify the people in the observance of the ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_758826587#7_1527251764","rank":6,"relevance":3}]},"time":3},"model_calls":62,"document_judgments":44,"relevance_3":31,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
